   "reply": "I put your plan into mojulo as a house and furnished the three rooms you asked for, but I haven't looked at any of the renders, so I can't say how they look. The house is at `/sketches/sk_f8u1c1kg0k`. I entered the rooms as drawn, with the lounge, kitchen and dining along the top, the hallway across the middle, and the two bedrooms and bathroom below. I let mojulo place the doors itself, so they may not match yours. Each room design is a separate sketch over the house, so you can try other schemes without changing the plan.\n\n- **Living room** (`/sketches/sk_iubq170g29`): modern-organic with wabi-sabi touches, so natural timber, soft upholstery and an earthy palette. It has a media console and TV on the hallway wall, an armchair, side table and floor lamp for reading, and a bookcase. The automatic layout wouldn't place the sofa because it blocked the kitchen door. I put it in by hand, with a coffee table and rug, facing the TV. The room's readout still lists the seating and rug as gaps, so check the sofa placement when you open it.\n- **Dining room** (`/sketches/sk_soa4fokoco`): modern farmhouse with warm-minimal accents. It has a 7-foot farmhouse table with six Windsor chairs on a rug, a sideboard and a bookcase, and the table faces the big east windows.\n- **Big bedroom** (`/sketches/sk_aa07a5ak73`): warm-minimal, with a king bed (trimmed to 2000 mm wide to fit the bed size range) flanked by two nightstands, plus a rug, a dresser, a sideboard, and an armchair with a floor lamp. It's arranged to look out the south windows.\n\nAll three rooms currently read as under-lit, with only the ceiling light and at most one lamp, so adding lamps would help the cozy feel. I can try other styles, swap the pieces around, or do the kitchen and the smaller bedroom next."
  },
