   "reply": "Yes, the dining room can seat eight, but it's a tight fit and it cost us the sideboard. I updated the design at `/sketches/sk_soa4fokoco`, though I haven't looked at the render.\n\nThe room is about 13.5 × 15.5 ft. The table is now 2740 mm (about 9 ft) long and 1000 mm wide, with eight Windsor chairs around it. I asked for a 2400 mm table, but mojulo stretched it to 2740 mm to fit eight seats. The rug grew to match.\n\n- **Sideboard:** it's gone. With the bigger table, no bare wall had room for it, and the layout flags this as a gap. I also removed the bookcase to free up space. If you want storage in here, a slim shelf or a console in the kitchen doorway area is the thing to try next.\n- **Lighting:** the room still has only its ceiling light, so a pendant over the table or a wall sconce would help the warm, cozy feel.\n\nFor parties with more than eight, the lounge seating could handle the overflow, or the table could move toward the east windows. I can try either."
  },
